---
import ArtworkMeta from "../../components/art/ArtworkMeta.astro";
---

<div class="mt-4 max-w-3xl">
  <ArtworkMeta fields={[
    { label: "Year", value: "2020" },
    { label: "Medium", value: "Mixed Media" },
    { label: "With", value: "Humanist.us × Wasawat Somno" },
  ]} />

  <p class="mb-4">
    The Territory is a representation and is often talked about and discussed the topic of sovereignty. It is neither truth nor fact, just a representation, but it affects the real world in terms of control and governing. What if the territory is not static but dynamic and still active since it's established? And what if it tries to expand its boundary like a tentacular being trying to seize and consume the new space?
  </p>

  <p class="mb-4">
    Tentacular Territoria is a set of 2 pieces that explore the territory, terrain, and technology, and how we perceive maps and the real world differently in each individual.
  </p>

  <div class="art-media-grid" style="max-width: 560px;">
    <img src="/images/tentacular-territoria/tentacular-territoria-1.jpg" alt="Tentacular Territoria — installation view" class="art-media-full" />
    <img src="/images/tentacular-territoria/tentacular-territoria-2.jpg" alt="Tentacular Territoria — contour lines projected on the floor" style="height: 180px; object-fit: cover;" />
    <img src="/images/tentacular-territoria/tentacular-territoria-3.jpg" alt="Tentacular Territoria — projection on draped fabric terrain" style="height: 180px; object-fit: cover;" />
    <img src="/images/tentacular-territoria/tentacular-territoria-4.jpg" alt="Tentacular Territoria — monitor showing a bot wandering through Google Maps" style="height: 180px; object-fit: cover;" />
    <img src="/images/tentacular-territoria/tentacular-territoria-5.jpg" alt="Enlighten exhibition signage listing artists and designers" style="height: 180px; object-fit: cover;" />
  </div>
</div>
